<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<ContentPage xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/maui/design"
             xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
             xmlns:i18n="clr-namespace:I18N_L10N.Extensions;assembly=I18N_L10N"
             mc:Ignorable="d"
             x:Class="Plutus.Frontend.AppClient.Views.MainTill.StoreOptions.StoreOptionsView"
             Title="{Binding Title}"
             IconImageSource="{Binding Icon, Converter={StaticResource MaterialIconConverter}}">
    <!--
      ⚠⚠ REBUILT 2026-08-17 TO MATCH THE WEB TILL. Matt: "MAUI looks nothing like the webtill."

      What was here, and why each piece went:

      * A LightGray top bar bound to `Store.StoreName` / `ReadableAddress` / `ContactNumber` /
        `VatIN` — the LEGACY `StoreModel`, which cutover step 20 made non-authoritative. On a
        portal-provisioned till that model is EMPTY, so the band rendered as a grey strip with
        nothing in it, above the same four facts fetched properly from the platform. It was not a
        layout problem, it was the old source of truth still on screen.
      * A "Region" panel printing `CultureInfo.FirstDayOfWeek` and a currency FORMAT STRING
        ("£###,###.##/-£###,###.##"). Neither is a fact about the shop and the web till shows
        neither; the second is developer output on an operator's screen.
      * A two-column Grid reflowed by `OnSizeAllocated`, which the cards' own wrapping replaces.

      ⚠ The body is still built in CODE (see the view model). That is deliberate and predates this
      change: the values come from an async fetch, and a XAML binding to a property that is not
      there renders as a SILENT BLANK on MAUI — no error, no warning, just an empty screen that
      looks designed. Code-built labels cannot fail that way.
    -->
    <ContentPage.Content>
        <ScrollView>
            <VerticalStackLayout x:Name="Body" Padding="16" Spacing="12" />
        </ScrollView>
    </ContentPage.Content>
</ContentPage>
